# ^ The official-pikafish/Pikafish source commit for the xiangqi Pikafish bot
# (scripts/engine-assets.sh reads the first line; this comment is ignored).
# `Pikafish dev-20260919-6a59ee2f`, upstream master.
# Applied unedited: pikafish-cc0-net.patch (sha256
# 790609318c020e3aeeb71a76ee7e987ee346d66005bb5eb26675544b2182d10b).
# The patch replaces the upstream evaluator with a reader for the public CC0
# Fairy-Stockfish net xiangqi-c07e94a5c7cb.nnue and disables net downloads.
# engine-assets.sh fetches that net from its pinned public source, checks its
# sha256, requires its NNUE info line, and gates bench 16 1 13 default depth on
# 1650882 nodes. The release ships the patch beside COPYING, never the net.
# The source pin stays unchanged; this patched evaluator changes behaviour.
#
# Pinned 2026-09-23. Until then the image did `git clone --depth 1` of upstream
# master on every deploy, so the bot was whatever Pikafish had merged that day
# (the reproducibility hole pikafish-jieqi.ref describes). This commit is the
# one production was running when the engines moved to prebuilt release assets,
# so the pin itself changed nothing about how the bot plays.
#
# Bumping is a behaviour change to a live bot, not just an upgrade: Pikafish's
# search and net move between commits. Change the SHA, let the Build engines
# workflow publish the new release, deploy, then re-run the EvE calibration for
# the xiangqi Pikafish rungs so their ratings are measured on the new binary.
